### Q2: residue+tiebreak witness for regular T_5, and is it speed-realizable? ###
  residue multisets (with some tie-break) giving regular T_5: 38
   ... require a parked residue 0: 1/38
   ... have all-distinct residues: 0/38
   ... rely on a margin-0 tie pair (tie-break dependent): 38/38
   sample witnesses (residue multiset, tie pairs):
      (0, 0, 0, 0, 0) ties: [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4), (3, 4)]
      (1, 1, 1, 1, 1) ties: [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4), (3, 4)]
      (1, 1, 1, 1, 13) ties: [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4), (3, 4)]
      (1, 1, 1, 13, 13) ties: [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4), (3, 4)]
      (1, 1, 13, 13, 13) ties: [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4), (3, 4)]
      (1, 13, 13, 13, 13) ties: [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4), (3, 4)]
      (2, 2, 2, 2, 2) ties: [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4), (3, 4)]
      (2, 2, 2, 2, 12) ties: [(0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4), (3, 4)]

  CLEAN witnesses (distinct nonzero residues, no tie dependence): 0
   => EVERY regular-T_5 witness needs EITHER a parked residue 0, OR repeated residues, OR a tie-break.
   This explains why generic primitive speed sets (distinct residues, no parking) avoid it.

